# Kconfig for NoMount

config NOMOUNT
	tristate "NoMount Path Redirection Subsystem"
	depends on KEYS
	default n
	help
	  NoMount allows path redirection and virtual file injection
	  without mounting filesystems. It uses the kernel keyring interface
	  to receive commands from its userspace companion. This operates at
	  the VFS layer; enable only on kernels intended to support NoMount.
